// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every index from 0 to just before the specified index, each element in the list is either null and was null before, or remains unchanged from its previous state.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every valid index less than the specified index, either both the current and old values at that index are null, or the current value at that index is equal to its old value.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every index i from 0 up to but not including the specified index, either both the current and previous values at i are null, or the current value at i is equal to the previous value at i.
--------------------
